diff --git a/docs/pocketforge-a133-peripheral-stubs.md b/docs/pocketforge-a133-peripheral-stubs.md
index 311c650..cd0eb09 100644
--- a/docs/pocketforge-a133-peripheral-stubs.md
+++ b/docs/pocketforge-a133-peripheral-stubs.md
@@ -61,3 +61,15 @@ bounded software register bank: IRQ enable `0x40..0x44`, W1C IRQ status
 Unmodelled registers read zero and ignore writes. Stored regulator values are
 guest-programmed state, not hardware measurements; the model generates no
 PMIC events and exposes no interrupt output.
+
+### MMC0 promotion
+
+MMC0 at `0x04020000`, SPI 39 is now the
+`allwinner-sdhost-sun50i-a100` functional model and accepts one raw SD drive
+on bus 0. The A100 subtype uses 8 KiB IDMA descriptors, exposes the sample
+delay calibration register, and reconstructs the word-addressed DLBA,
+descriptor buffer, and next-descriptor fields before applying the four-byte
+alignment mask. MMC1 remains an inert register stub and disabled MMC2 remains
+absent. The qtest reads LBA 1 through IDMA from both a valid GPT marker and a
+corrupt control image, and checks that a command with no attached medium gets
+no response.
